course: dictionary
lesson: 1415
title: Carelessly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Carelessly is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, and it comes from the word careless. When you do something carelessly, you do not take enough care or attention, so mistakes or accidents can happen. Many adverbs end in -ly, so look out for them in a text.
explain: Careless can mean two things. Sometimes it means you are not paying attention. Other times it means you are relaxed and not worried. «She tossed her bag carelessly onto the bed» shows she did not stop to put it down neatly.
explain: Use the context to decide which meaning fits. In a maths test, working carelessly can lead to copying a number wrong. Swap in "without care" and check whether the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Carelessly means without enough care or attention.
fact: Careless is the root word, and carelessly is its adverb form.
fact: Carelessly can also mean in a relaxed way that shows you are not worried.
fact: In «The Wind in the Willows», the Rat «incautiously» tells Toad that the Mole and the Badger «will be out till luncheon time», so Toad knows he will be alone with the Rat.
fact: Phrases you will meet include drive carelessly, carelessly left, and handle knives carelessly.
exercise: «She tossed her bag carelessly onto the bed.» What does carelessly mean here? | Very neatly and slowly | *In a relaxed way, without caring where it landed | Quietly, so nobody could hear | Angrily, after a long argument
exercise: Ali worked carelessly and wrote 74 instead of 47. What does carelessly suggest? | Careful and very slow | *Without enough care, so a mistake happened | Happy and singing | Planned for weeks
exercise: Which word means the same as carelessly? | Patiently | Carefully | *Without care | Slowly
test: Which sentence shows someone acting carelessly with safety? | *Running across the road without looking | Holding the rail on the stairs | Waiting at the kerb for the green man | Carefully checking both ways before crossing
test: In «The Wind in the Willows», the Rat says the Mole and the Badger «will be out till luncheon time». Why does Toad feel pleased? | *Because he will be alone with the Rat | Because he hates luncheon | Because it is raining | Because the Mole is his friend
exam: Which sentence uses carelessly correctly? | The carelessly bright lamp was on. | Carelessly the sun rose over the hill. | *He carelessly left the back gate open, and the dog ran out. | She carelessly checked every answer twice.
